  <note>
    <content>
      <p>RK24 froze an author-structure, train-only refit before model fitting. Published Boël coefficients were not used for prediction because they were fit on all E0/E5 source data. The 61 single-codon slopes and both author binary models were fit only on train E0/E5 by unregularized binary logistic regression; the multiclass models used all train rows and fixed L2 = 0.01 multinomial logistic regression. Train, development and test contain 5,079, 635 and 634 constructs. Test contains 398 E0/E5 rows in 364 binary protein clusters and 634 multiclass rows in 556 protein clusters. Inference used 20,000 protein-cluster bootstrap replicates and 20,000 within-cluster prediction-swap permutations.</p>
      <p>On test, base and author binary AUC are 0.600905137540453 and 0.7882281553398058; the gain is 0.1873230177993528 with 95% interval 0.13324636329372375 to 0.2421234519153588. Base and author binary log-loss are 0.6847873019746681 and 0.5538465767221601; the improvement is 0.130940725252508 with interval 0.08246948450936671 to 0.17778180644415129. Base and author multiclass Spearman are 0.12858011330132996 and 0.4305908753425497; the gain is 0.30201076204121974 with interval 0.22739420732548424 to 0.37520097036757444. Base and author multiclass MSE are 4.331129372215796 and 3.5592915124691085; the improvement is 0.7718378597466873 with interval 0.5630600690157701 to 0.9837873937534691. Every Holm-adjusted p value is 0.000199990000499975 and all four primary endpoints pass.</p>
      <p>The pre-registered supplementary HistGB comparison is descriptive only and does not change the four-endpoint Gate. Frozen RK23 HistGB plus UH test Spearman is 0.20073508224367628 and author multiclass Spearman is 0.4305908753425497; the descriptive gain is 0.2298557930988734. HistGB MSE is 4.326145966453431 and author MSE is 3.5592915124691085; the descriptive improvement is 0.766854453984323. The RK24 base logistic predictions are value-identical to the frozen RK23 base plus UH predictions.</p>
      <p>Independent acceptance passed 153 of 153 checks after rebuilding every author feature, refitting all 61 single-codon models and four final models, and reconstructing train, development and test predictions, metrics, bootstrap arrays and permutation arrays without importing the production modules. Maximum static-feature difference is 7.216449660063518e-16; maximum prediction difference is 2.4740689497093626e-09; maximum metric difference is 5.4017679218532066e-11; maximum bootstrap difference is 3.0417401930549204e-10; maximum permutation difference is 2.1483925749521404e-10. Development independent acceptance separately passed 97 of 97 checks. The retained history includes the pre-fit label-field correction, a verifier-only metric-count correction, and a test-verifier command-line argument correction; none changed the frozen scientific protocol or outputs.</p>
      <p>The supported conclusion is limited to superiority of the train-only Boël author-structure model over the frozen base plus UH comparator on this reused cross-protein, non-synonymous ordinal-expression split. This is not fixed-protein synonymous causality, research OOD, translation velocity, mRNA decay, full spatial coupling, functional untouched confirmation, CodonFlow-RK generation or external SOTA. RK-G1 remains false, expensive generator training remains unauthorized, and functional untouched data were not accessed (frozen test evidence commit b4c04d2935015386603a5dff8b1f8c9247295b5a; scientific closeout commit a35097243e9b0f2b71786479bd981488ac3ed526).</p>
    </content>
